{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review","id":1538031,"title":"W5 Red Tundra - Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-03T03:46:41-07:00","id":1538031,"title":"W5 Red Tundra - Review","content":"<b>Red Tundra</b> is a W5 adventure that was released by Renegade for Free RPG Day. It\u2019s supposed to be an introductory adventure people can run at a game-store to familiarize people with W5. That\u2019s what it\u2019s supposed to do.<br /> <br /> To lay my cards on the table right up front: It doesn\u2019t achieve that goal. It\u2019s clear the writer has only a passing familiarity with WtA at best but worse than that\u2026 it\u2019s badly written. Reading through the adventure reminded me of sitting through truly bad movies like Morbius or Gods of Egypt\u2026 these bad movies where characters act weird and things happen in ways that make little sense or it\u2019s hard to fathom what rhyme or reason is underlying any of the creative decisions. Maybe the writer was rushed or something in their personal life distracted them but the adventure is just\u2026 bad. This is the worst one of the ones I\u2019ve reviewed thus far, I think.<br /> <br /> The book starts with an introduction of the setting to familiarize everyone with W5. It introduces the idea of werewolves and Garou in its basics as well as the Auspices with one or two sentences. But the most interesting aspect of the Introduction is the section called \u201cThe Apocalypse Is Now\u201d. I and many others had discussions on this forum about the state of the world in the W5 setting. And it\u2019s interesting to put the \u201cAge of Apocalypse\u201d in the context of V5\u2019s idea of a \u201ccyclical Gehenna\u201d. Here, though, this all gets dispelled in a way that I found almost too matter-of-fact.<br /> <br /> What the section describes is that the Apocalypse in W5 is the actual physical and spiritual destruction of the world. It\u2019s the literal end of the world. And you get descriptions about that like \u201cIt\u2019s not a question of faith.\u201d. But where it gets weird is when you get a section like \u201cSometimes the Garou call this the war against the Wyrm, but the true cause of the destruction is not in the spirit world. It\u2019s right here. The only question is, what can be done about it? This torments the Garou. They can kill a corrupt cop possessed by a Bane, a Wyrm Spirit. But can they stop a vast corporation from logging in the Amazon?\u201d. That almost makes it seem like caring about the Umbra, the Triat and Spirits is a distraction and Garou instead should just deal with humanity directly in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Then we get the introduction to the setting and the core-concept of this adventure. The setting is a small town in Northwestern Canada called Winter Creek. But this is where the strange/bad writing starts to appear. So the idea is that all the PCs are from this area and the human-born characters all went to the same school. But because the town is suffering from massive unemployment, they all left for the big city \u2013 but now they\u2019re coming back. Also, there are wolfborn characters who stayed behind but somehow have fully integrated into human society. But also in the past they all joined the one Pack that operated in the city called the Lunabombers (terrible name) who is led by this hyper-aggressive Red Talon Ahroun called Marcus Oakheart. But before the PCs left for the big city, they also had a falling-out with Oakheart and founded their own Pack called\u2026 The Band (again, another terrible name). And now they\u2019re back because\u2026 I have no idea. They\u2019re just back. And the wolfborn Pack-members also supposedly never left but somehow are still part of the Pack\u2026 Look, it makes no sense. But the idea is that the PC-Pack has some history with the region, they left and now they\u2019re back.<br /> <br /> The book comes with six ready-made characters who are the PC-Pack (two of whom are wolfborn) and oh boy\u2026 what a group. But I will get to that at the end.<br /> <br /> Then the book introduces the most important characters in the adventure. And the one character-description that should be highlighted here is Tucha. This is what it says in the description: \u201cShe is a builder and a problem-solver, making nests and even cleverly disarming simple traps with her claws.\u201d The thing is\u2026 I left out the beginning which says that this is supposed to describe a wolf Kin before its First Change. And then it says stuff like \u201cShe will appear in the form of a black-haired woman in her thirties and her understanding of human society is based on past observations as a wolf.\u201d. Also the image that goes along with this is of a black woman in her thirties with dreadlocks, tattoos and earrings\u2026 which doesn\u2019t really fit the idea of what\u2019s described. The drawing looks way too much like a person who\u2019s already fully part of human society.<br /> <br /> In the description of Marcus Oakheart we also find out that he has fallen to Hauglosk which means\u2026 he\u2019s really grumpy and angry. And the only other member of his Pack that is mentioned is a Red Talon Philodox named Jana Goodhowl. Again, just a weird character. This is what it says in her description: \u201cIronically, her habit of avoiding conflict is perhaps what has kept her so close to Marcus Oakheart even after his descent into Hauglosk: she is afraid to confront his extreme views and to remind him of the tenets of the Litany.\u201d And what makes it even weirder is how she appears in the adventure but we\u2019ll get to that\u2026<br /> <br /> Before, Hauglosk was strongly tied to rightwing extremist beliefs which was odd but here it\u2019s another kind of odd. Because the way it\u2019s described during the adventure is that the Lunabombers-Pack-members and the PC Pack\u2026 they all know he\u2019s suffering from Hauglosk but they all just accept it with a shrug a la \u201cHey, what can you do\u2026?\u201d. It\u2019s accepted that he will make bad decisions because of Hauglosk but nobody feels compelled to deal with it beyond knowing that this will happen. It feels like it\u2019s treated like a kind of dementia, some sort of mental illness that nobody can do anything about. The best you can do is operate around that Garou\u2019s erratic behavior. I guess, it\u2019s closer to how it\u2019s described in Deepest of Wounds where the Cult of Fenris members may have different opinions but there\u2019s no open hostility between them and the other Garou (at least until the kidnapping is uncovered). And if Oakheart and Jana don\u2019t die during this adventure, they are willing to work together with the PC Pack if they want to stay (although on \u201cstrained terms\u201d as the book describes it).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter One</span><br /> <br /> The PCs arrive in town and to showcase taking tests, the first scene that is set up here is\u2026 to evade the Pastor. Because he\u2019s annoying. But anyway, besides that the real goal at this point is for the characters to meet up with coach MacKenzie. Remember how I mentioned that all the human-born characters went to the same school? One assumption in the adventure is that all the human-born characters REALLY care about this coach from their highschool. In fact, the adventure makes the coach the Touchstone for all the human-born characters. (Even though part of the premise is that the human-born characters had left the small town for the big city\u2026)<br /> <br /> The characters go to the meeting-place but\u2026 BAM! Marcus Oakheart in Crinos Form attacks the PC-Pack. Somehow nobody\u2019s around, so the Veil stays intact\u2026 yeah, \u201csomehow\u201d, sure\u2026 There\u2019s a fight but after two rounds Jana Goodhowl appears and calms Oakheart down. She has a special Talisman whistle, you see, that can end Frenzy and the Spirits blessed her with being super-persuasive or something. It\u2019s weird. The Talisman is called \u201cDogwhistle of Control: Blowing in this whistle calms any targeted Garou for a turn, no matter how consumed by Rage or Hauglosk, forcing them to consider their actions and listen to reason. [ \u2026 ] The talisman has been granted by the spirits to Jana Goodhowl specifically. It won\u2019t cooperate with anyone else.\u201d As a side-note, the Marcus and Jana have Gifts listed for them and the text is copy-pasted from the W5 corebook. The problem is that Gifts rely on specific Renown traits and neither of these two has their Renown-traits listed. So, here for example she has the Ancestral Conviction Gift which adds Honor as bonus dice to any attempt to convince other Garou. But it\u2019s nowhere listed what Jana\u2019s Honor-rating is. The same happened with Marcus Oakheart and his Gifts. It\u2019s a bit of an oversight.<br /> <br /> The following dialogue between Jana, Marcus and the PCs suggested by the adventure is also weird. Here\u2019s a snippet:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThere\u2019s no reason to spill Garou blood tonight.\u201d, Jana says as much to you as her leader. \u201cTry to remember, Marcus and the rest of you as well. These are the tenets of the Litany: Respect the territory of another, the Veil shall not be lifted and the leader may not be challenged during wartime. So please, what are you doing here?\u201d<br /> You aren\u2019t sure if this is wartime and Oakheart is not your leader but perhaps that is a debate for another time. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would\u2019ve immediately called bullshit on this because Marcus attacked the PCs. The fault lies entirely with him.<br /> <br /> And then these two Garou are giving you exposition. There\u2019s a company called the FOMO Hunting Company and they\u2019re killing wolves in the region. They organize hunting-trips for rich people as well to shoot wolves from helicopters. And then they ask the PC-Pack to help them with the attack. The turn-about happens really fast. First, Marcus attacks the PCs, then Jana shows up and acts like the PCs and Marcus are equally to blame and then they try to ally themselves with the PCs while giving an exposition-dump about who the bad guys are. It\u2019s not a good scene\u2026<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn\u2019t it be kinda hard to shoot moving wolves while being in the air in an also moving helicopter? It sounds more like a challenge than something you\u2019d wanna do for fun.<br /> <br /> Or take Jana\u2019s characterization\u2026 just a couple pages ago it said she\u2019s afraid of confrontation and won\u2019t mention the Litany to Oakheart and here in the very first scene she\u2019s doing exactly that. If anything, this scene would make me think Jana is the Pack leader and not Oakheart.<br /> <br /> Then the characters proceed to the Silver Saloon which is the local bar where they\u2019re supposed to meet the coach. He isn\u2019t there yet and the book offers options for the characters to investigate what\u2019s up. The one option that stood out to me here is the question of \u201cIs it legal to kill wolves?\u201d. And the adventure offers this 200-word sidebar giving a detailed answer on the real-world situation. But this is WtA\u2026 of course, it\u2019s bad and has to be stopped. I mean, what, are the PCs supposed to think \u201cHey, how about we draft a lawsuit against the corporation instead of attacking the Fomori working for them?\u201d. It\u2019s so hard for me to imagine that in this setup, a player would organically wonder whether what the evil villain is doing is legal. It\u2019s the villain! Of course, it\u2019s not supposed to be a good thing! And you\u2019re never going to deal with a Fomor-boss by dragging them to a court to convict them! That\u2019s not what WtA is about\u2026<br /> <br /> So you meet the coach except\u2026 he\u2019s not a coach anymore. He lost his job and is now working for\u2026 FOMO Hunting Company! Oh no! You can interrogate this character but it\u2019s a bit weird because he doesn\u2019t have that much new information to offer. And other things you can learn in different ways later on. You can even try to convince him to just call in sick the next day as you go after the company. It\u2019s assumed that the PCs should be very invested in keeping the coach safe.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter Two</span><br /> <br /> The adventure now has a distinct Day 1 and Day 2 for dealing with the company. Chapter Two deals with Day 1 (which is also the day before the hunt happens) and this is the best part of the adventure because it explicitly explores various routes the characters can take in making Day 2 easier for themselves while also making sure innocents have been protected/forewarned.<br /> <br /> But the weirdest part is the one route where the PC Pack contact the Trout Lake pack. Because you see, this adventure seems to believe that wolves have human-level intelligence. You\u2019re going to the Lake Trout pack as one of the options to warn them that they\u2019re going to be the target of the hunt the next day. And it\u2019s described like this: \u201cAnd then you can already smell one of their guards, a young male. You howl a little to make your presence known and soon you hear a reply that you should prepare to meet Nahanni. The leader walks majestically on a hilltop, the moon illuminating her outline. She looks down upon you and growls \u201cWhy have you come?\u201d \u201c. And then you can only communicate with Nahanni in Lupus or Hispo Form. Because the description I just quoted there isn\u2019t for wolfborn Garou but for normal wolves! They even have names!<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s a sidebar on Kinseeking. As mentioned before, there\u2019s this character called Tucho who is a wolf-kin in that pack. And the sidebar says stuff like \u201cBut they can try to force Tucho\u2019s First Change by attacking her or by changing form in front of her..\u201d Also, PCs can just sniff her out or use the Gift Sense The True Form. That isn\u2019t the case elsewhere. There\u2019s one specific Rite in the corebook to enable the ability to detect Kin. But the way it\u2019s handled here, you wouldn\u2019t even need the Rite.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter Three</span><br /> <br /> This is the day when the hunt happens and the book really let\u2019s itself off the hook here. You get an hour by hour play-by-play of what would happen on that day if the PCs had done nothing and weren\u2019t around. Essentially Oakheart and the Lunabombers attack a Lodge, kill some people, the Fomori take off in a helicopter and kill the wolves at Lake Trout. Oakheart and his Pack retreat, licking their wounds and mourning their failures. And then you just get this section called \u201cWhat Really Happens\u201d which gives a couple examples of what may change due to what PCs had done in the previous chapter and how they could influence the described events. It\u2019s VERY free-form.<br /> <br /> And then it just goes to the conclusion and aftermath. If Oakheart is still alive, you can start a Sept between the PC-Pack and the Lunabombers. And I guess, Oakheart\u2019s Hauglosk is just\u2026 not a big deal. Also, somehow the PCs attack against the FOMO hunting company gets it in trouble. And if the coach is still alive, he\u2019s out of a job again because of that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">The PCs</span><br /> <br /> You get six ready-made characters and the book even occasionally mentions how they could be relevant in particular sections of the adventure. All well and good but these guys\u2026 that\u2019s one hell of a group.<br /> <br /> Especially because whoever filled out the char-sheets must have read the character-creation-section with their eyes closed.<br /> <br /> First, the characters are imbalanced. Some are stronger than others. You have one, for example, with 16 dots in Attributes in total and then another with 11. Second, the characters are badly designed for new players. Normally you have three Gifts and one Rite at character-creation. There\u2019s one character with three Gifts and five Rites. The other have around six Gifts and Rites usually. Third, there are straight up mistakes being made. One character has a Spirit Pact Background with zero dots in it, for example. No explanation as to what it\u2019s even supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> It's a mess!<br /> <br /> But let\u2019s talk about the character-concepts itself:<br /> <br /> Shelley \u201cMoonshadow\u201d Le Borgne (human born Shadow Lord Galliard): She plays ice hockey. And she had her First Change during a game. It says \u201cIf not for the ice skates and the padding, she might have murdered both teams.\u201d\u2026 Not sure, what exactly happened here. Also, part of her concept is that she plays ice hockey by day and \u201cby night she prowls the streets, teaching the songs of the moon to other werewolves.\u201d So why would she go back to Winter Creek\u2026? Who knows\u2026<br /> <br /> Darius Van Detta (wolf born Black Fury Theurge): He constantly fought with his wolf-pack before his First Change and so he was driven out. Then he fought with human hunters and realized the Wyrm was the true enemy. That\u2019s when his First Change happened and now he\u2019s somehow really knowledgeable about spirits.<br /> <br /> Ida \u201cRatbrain\u201d Fong (human born Bone Gnawer Ragabash): She was an obedient straight-A student but she was always curious. She became a journalist and that\u2019s when she realized just how bad the world around her was. That\u2019s when her First Change happened. But I just love the last line of the description. So weird! \u201cOn the way, she has also become a disillusioned big city drug addict who has drifted more and more into marginalia with her strange opinions and attitudes.\u201d \u2018Disillusioned big city drug addict\u2019\u2026 what a phrase!<br /> <br /> Ashley \u201cFernfur\u201d Greeneyes (wolf born Hart Warden Ahroun): Another weird wolf-description here\u2026 \u201cAshley grew up a wolf, one of those wolves who loved the territory of their pack and did their utmost to protect its flora and fauna.\u201d Ah, so that\u2019s what wolves are up to, I see. But now I really wanna meet \u201cone of those wolves\u201d that don\u2019t like their territory\u2026 Anyway, her territory got attacked, she underwent First Change and\u2026 attacked the humans in her new human Form. Then it says \u201cHumans recognized her as Indigenous and she adopted the name of Ashley Greeneyes.\u201d The phrasing is just so odd. They recognized her as \u201cIndigenous\u201d (?) and her name is \u201cAshley\u201d\u2026?<br /> <br /> Jonas \u201cSparks\u201d Beaulieu (human born Glass Walkers Philodox): He likes machines. That\u2019s why he\u2019s a Glass Walker. But what about him being a Philodox, you may wonder\u2026 \u201cAfter he changed, he felt a strange need to delve deep into the history and customs of the Garou as well as the laws of Canada, the territories and the reserve, becoming an impromptu arbitrator in many disputes.\u201d I think this takes Auspice a bit too literal\u2026 You don\u2019t need to become a lawyer just because you had your First Change under the half-moon.<br /> <br /> Jared Tierney (human born Galestalkers Ahroun): It starts like this \u201cJared may not have the book smarts but he has heart.\u201d What is the concept? Well, it all revolves around him having a dark little secret\u2026 He killed his entire family during his First Change and then ran away. As a concept, it\u2019s way too dark in my opinion. The only bright spot is that if there\u2019s room, this is the last character anyone would wanna pick from the six pre-made ones. The reason is simple: He has the weakest char-sheet by far compared to the other ones. Four of his attributes have 1 dot and only one Attribute is a four-dot. It\u2019s like the author hated this character or something.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Conclusion</span><br /> <br /> It\u2019s the worst one so far. The character-motivations are strange, their descriptions even stranger and the scenario feels a bit half-baked. And then add to that the weird ready-made characters. There\u2019s really nothing here that would make me think you would get anything out of this.<br /> <br /> And the wolves! Hopefully, it\u2019s just this one weird writer who convinced themselves that wolves are sacred nature protectors with human-level intelligence (even without a First Change) in the W5 setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T07:46:09-07:00","id":1538043,"title":"","content":"The helicopter wolf shooting sadly IS a thing, used to collar them OR to kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T13:55:51-07:00","id":1538056,"title":"","content":"Does the author think that hockey gear can keep a Crinos-form Garou at bay, or that it covers them up harmlessly? Or is it that the teams managed to skate away faster than they could normally run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T14:51:57-07:00","id":1538057,"title":"","content":"The sapient Wolves thing would actually make sense in a Legacy product with Kinfolk Wolves being much more near-human intellect. In W5 they're just Wolves even if Kin.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling to see after all these depictions of Hauglosk in Renegade products as ' slightly more grumpy' or ' slightly more likely to believe stupid things about different groups of humans' but still less extreme in actual action than the two example Red Talons from the Core why it necessitates removing the PC from player control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T19:58:22-07:00","id":1538069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538057#post1538057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sapient Wolves thing would actually make sense in a Legacy product with Kinfolk Wolves being much more near-human intellect. In W5 they're just Wolves even if Kin.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling to see after all these depictions of Hauglosk in Renegade products as ' slightly more grumpy' or ' slightly more likely to believe stupid things about different groups of humans' but still less extreme in actual action than the two example Red Talons from the Core why it necessitates removing the PC from player control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's some form of miscommunication among writers and parawolf and I suspect that parawolf doesn't provide the writing team with actual guidelines on most of the lore the corebook lays out means. <br /> <br /> Fan made projects like Werewolf the essentials by contrast seems to have a much more solid grasp on the lore from the little preview material I've seen..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T00:17:52-07:00","id":1538071,"title":"","content":"One thing I've noticed, which is actually really good, the wolf-born are being used much more than lupus were in Legacy. Even if their concepts are &quot;wolf trying to be human&quot;, the wolf-born aren't put to the sidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T01:39:15-07:00","id":1538072,"title":"","content":"It would certainly change things a bit for how wolfborn Garou can be portrayed if they continue to portray normal wolves like they're characters from The Lion King. At that point, the jump from wolf to Garou after the First Change isn't that big anymore. It loses a bit of the flavor from previous editions, I think, but it would certainly justify the approach from the W5 corebook to not really care about the difference between wolf-born and human-born.<br /> <br /> Also, one thing I've noticed is that they love to give wolf-born characters the Illiterate Flaw. It's partly due to how the WOD5E system demands you to pick Flaws during character-creation, I guess, but I wish we could get something more flavorful and wolf-born specific. Especially because the way the Illiterate Flaw works is &quot;Flaw: (\u2022\u2022) Illiterate: You cannot read or write. Your Academics and Science Skills are capped at 1, and you can have no Specialty in them that incorporates modern knowledge.&quot; Capping Skills is a bit harsh. And sure, you can always negotiate with the ST to remove the Flaw during the chronicle for justified story-reasons but that's one of those Flaws that I think should be worth more than two dots (in the same way that Jared's Dark Secret Flaw as a one-dot-thing feels too low as well). But that's more of an overall problem with the WOD5E system. It's mandated to pick Flaws but the offering you can choose from is pretty small in number.<br /> <br /> Another thing I forgot to mention is that the wolfborn characters have Nahanni, the wolf who leads the Lake Trout pack, as their Touchstone. And it's said the two wolfborn came from that Pack. But then Darius' backstory talks about how he challenged his wolf-pack-leader too many times and got kicked out of the pack (that's all before his First Change). It's just strange because that would be Nahanni in that case. I guess that's yet another thing that wasn't really thought through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T03:00:49-07:00","id":1538075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538071#post1538071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've noticed, which is actually really good, the wolf-born are being used much more than lupus were in Legacy. Even if their concepts are &quot;wolf trying to be human&quot;, the wolf-born aren't put to the sidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were? Lupus NPCs are fairly common in Legacy....though Crinosborn NPCs are over-represented compared to population numbers it's true. Still a solid proportion of the most important Garou in the world are Lupusborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T03:13:02-07:00","id":1538076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538072#post1538072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would certainly change things a bit for how wolfborn Garou can be portrayed if they continue to portray normal wolves like they're characters from The Lion King. At that point, the jump from wolf to Garou after the First Change isn't that big anymore. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrast to the wolf born character from book of hungry names. Who from what I've heard (never played the game myself) has a weird thought process compared to humans. Like to an outside observer she's somewhere on the spectrum but the narrative make it pretty clear that she's pretty normal and most of her oddities is just a wolf having trouble grasping human subjects. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T05:16:05-07:00","id":1538079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538075#post1538075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were? Lupus NPCs are fairly common in Legacy....though Crinosborn NPCs are over-represented compared to population numbers it's true. Still a solid proportion of the most important Garou in the world are Lupusborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the same way as in W5. In W5 they are just there, in Legacy there was a higher bar for a lupus PC to get involved and even one the earliest chronicle books says that there shouldn't be too many lupus PCs. While having a comically bad crinos born template.<br /> <br /> In W5, it seems like the bar is much lower, which is interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T09:48:49-07:00","id":1538087,"title":"","content":"The hockey bit remembered me of the first WtA game I storytelled.<br /> Players were used to D&amp;D mostly, and this time roleplayed high school hockey players and didn't know we were playing WtA.<br /> <br /> When the time of the first match comes it's against the nastier and foulish team of the city (very few people on the stands to watch the game because no one really like the players on both teams).<br /> First Change explodes for everyone, but it was mostly &quot;everything fades black&quot;.<br /> I think there is no need to say that when they get back to themselves the scenario was basically a slaughterhouse.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that bit of &quot;If not for the ice skates and the padding, she might have murdered both teams&quot; sounded even more incredibly silly to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T18:33:50-07:00","id":1538107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538087#post1538087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeah, that bit of &quot;If not for the ice skates and the padding, she might have murdered both teams&quot; sounded even more incredibly silly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now to be fair a whole pack of garoues changing in a icerink is a really different from a lone wolf. Like if the new werewolf claws doesn't immediately find a solid grip in a slippery icerink floor then there's a chance that all the people on feld can escape and I could see the hockey gear turn a injury from some glancing blows from a raging crinos from lethal to crippled for life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T21:40:24-07:00","id":1538108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538079#post1538079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in the same way as in W5. In W5 they are just there, in Legacy there was a higher bar for a lupus PC to get involved and even one the earliest chronicle books says that there shouldn't be too many lupus PCs. While having a comically bad crinos born template.<br /> <br /> In W5, it seems like the bar is much lower, which is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nod towards lower Lupus numbers was in reference to wolves being hunted to the verge of extinction in most of the older Legacy material so that there was an imbalance ( noted by the Nation) of too many Homids drowning out Lupus voices and adding to the tension that drove Lupus into the arms of the Talons. None of thats really relevant to W5 where Lupus and Homids are interchangable and theres no tension between the Breeds at all......and no nation to speak of. <br /> <br /> Like Damian referenced I prefer the Lupus to be more valued and tension between the Garou of different origins though I appreciate that others may have other priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T23:27:44-07:00","id":1538110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538108#post1538108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Damian referenced I prefer the Lupus to be more valued and tension between the Garou of different origins though I appreciate that others may have other priorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is more that, due to their rarity and the stat debuff, lupus were not really given much of a chance to be anything but the local canid at times. With Red Talon-focused books there was more variety, but the feeling I constantly got was the writers struggling with the NPCs.<br /> <br /> with Wolf Born, I see the writers clearly feeling less pressure to write them. Which most likely is due to the lack of a debuff.<br /> <br /> I assume you cannot buy out a flaw in WoD5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T01:34:23-07:00","id":1538111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538110#post1538110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume you cannot buy out a flaw in WoD5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not during character-creation. Because of how this is structured (with the standard being that you pick two dots worth of Flaws) unlike other traits in WOD5E, Flaws don't have a range of 1 to 5 dots but rather of 1 or 2 dots. That's of course quite limiting in representing the degree of a flaw. Personally with that expectation, I always thought it would have been better to create categories of Minor and Major Flaws rather than thinking of it in dots. Because one dot in a Background is a small thing while one dot in a Flaw can be quite big. But that was baked in since V5. Of all the things, this has been something H5 and W5 left untouched.<br /> <br /> Additionally, V5 had that add-on for character-creation called &quot;The Sea of Time&quot; (pg 151) where you had three degrees of starting experience: Childer (nothing), Neonate (a decade or two of being a vampire; 15 XP) and then Ancilla (been around for near a century; dot of Blood Potence, 35 XP). Neither H5 nor W5 have anything like that. It's just some short remarks. I think the W5 corebook suggests at one point you could give more dots of Renown during character-creation for more experienced starting characters but there's no structure or examples for that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T02:13:47-07:00","id":1538114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538110#post1538110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is more that, due to their rarity and the stat debuff, lupus were not really given much of a chance to be anything but the local canid at times. With Red Talon-focused books there was more variety, but the feeling I constantly got was the writers struggling with the NPCs.<br /> <br /> with Wolf Born, I see the writers clearly feeling less pressure to write them. Which most likely is due to the lack of a debuff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well Bohn has of a wolf Born character named Min whose though process is pretty weird to an onlooker. Like the game make it clear that a wolf gaining human intellangce won't necessary think like a human. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T06:07:36-07:00","id":1538125,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to being kind of lost on awesome NPCs such as Scar Throat Leech-Killer, Seeks-the-Truth, Son-of-Moonlight, Bull Roarer and others being described as ' the local canid' and what 'debuff' is being talked about. The restriction on Ability selections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T07:03:33-07:00","id":1538130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538125#post1538125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit to being kind of lost on awesome NPCs such as Scar Throat Leech-Killer, Seeks-the-Truth, Son-of-Moonlight, Bull Roarer and others being described as ' the local canid' and what 'debuff' is being talked about. The restriction on Ability selections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for reminding me of them. I admit I was wrong on this.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the ability restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:03:18-07:00","id":1538308,"title":"","content":"While I was talking to a friend about W5 and looking through the W5 corebook, I noticed something. So Jane Goodhowl first appears in that scene where Marcus Oakheart attacks the players but she interrupts it with her Talisman called &quot;The Dogwhistle of Control&quot; (again, bad name... really every name the writers chose in this book is bad, that's kind of an achievement) and it says this: &quot;Blowing in this whistle calms any targeted Garou for a turn, no matter how consumed by Rage or Hauglosk, forcing them to consider their actions and listen to reason. [ \u2026 ] The talisman has been granted by the spirits to Jana Goodhowl specifically. It won\u2019t cooperate with anyone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's where it gets interesting: Technically that Talisman already existed in W5. It's called the &quot;Harmony Flute&quot; (pg 188)<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"518\" height=\"476\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/eNIY4JQ.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/eNIY4JQ.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/eNIY4JQ.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> The version presented in the Red Tundra is not only much stronger but makes less sense. That version does 1 Superficial WP-damage and makes a Garou lose 1 dot of Rage and presumably, the description implies some sort of mental command where the targeted Garou has to calmly consider their actions and listen to the owner of the &quot;dogwhistle&quot;. But in comparison, the &quot;Dogwhistle of Control&quot; feels more like a butchered version of the Harmony Flute. At least with the Harmony Flute the outline of what it does and how it works is pretty clear.<br /> <br /> Also, W5 already doesn't have a lot of Talismans to offer to players thus far, so to choose to create an alternate version of an already existing Talisman is baffling. And I suspect the reason the writer created this stronger version is entirely about using it as a crutch for the scene to unfold like it's described in the book. But this is another case of bad writing. This person wrote themselves into a corner by having a frenzied, Hauglosk-suffering Oakheart attack the PCs in Crinos-Form and then the only way the writer could think of getting out of that scene was by taking the &quot;Harmony Flute&quot; and based on that create that powerful &quot;Dogwhistle&quot; (which can shut down and change the trajectory of the scene in one turn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:22:22-07:00","id":1538316,"title":"","content":"All the Renegade material and the CYOA books have significant lore, metaphysics and rules deviations from the core. Red Tundra definitely has the worst writing on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:04:37-07:00","id":1538321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538316#post1538316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Renegade material and the CYOA books have significant lore, metaphysics and rules deviations from the core. Red Tundra definitely has the worst writing on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, that might be because they aren't too considerate of having one specific version and are giving the devs (mostly) free hands.<br /> <br /> I mean, the way hauglosk is treated here is VERY different from previous ones. That is why stuff like the CoF having only one tone stands out so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T21:56:37-07:00","id":1538343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538321#post1538321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh, that might be because they aren't too considerate of having one specific version and are giving the devs (mostly) free hands.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean Forsaken has taken a similar approach to the all they line books but they're pretty consistent a few unfortunate exceptions &quot;chough&quot; Changling Breeds &quot;chough&quot;. <br /> <br /> Though Onyx path relying on in house writers instead of outsourcing to another studio would have a impact on the quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T23:11:08-07:00","id":1538345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538343#post1538343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean Forsaken has taken a similar approach to the all they line books but they're pretty consistent a few unfortunate exceptions &quot;chough&quot; Changling Breeds &quot;chough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though Onyx path relying on in house writers instead of outsourcing to another studio would have a impact on the quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>CoD's Changing Breeds book was technically a side project for the blue &quot;mortal&quot; line, not a proper Forsaken book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T00:19:45-07:00","id":1538347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538343#post1538343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean Forsaken has taken a similar approach to the all they line books but they're pretty consistent a few unfortunate exceptions &quot;chough&quot; Changling Breeds &quot;chough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though Onyx path relying on in house writers instead of outsourcing to another studio would have a impact on the quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and because things were in-house people spoke to one another or just knew the tone they had to hit.<br /> <br /> W5 will forever suffer from trying to be more 'werewolf' and still having the Apocalypse plot required. Because there are times you just want to do 'werewolf' and not 'eternity war.' W5 has the tools to just go werewolf, it should have adventures that give players a traditional werewolf experience.<br /> <br /> But it can't because the apocalypse is tacked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T00:50:03-07:00","id":1538348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538347#post1538347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That and because things were in-house people spoke to one another or just knew the tone they had to hit.<br /> <br /> W5 will forever suffer from trying to be more 'werewolf' and still having the Apocalypse plot required. Because there are times you just want to do 'werewolf' and not 'eternity war.' W5 has the tools to just go werewolf, it should have adventures that give players a <b>traditional werewolf experience.</b><br /> <br /> But it can't because the apocalypse is tacked on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that such a thing exists. Every work is different, and few of them agree. Now, there's the Hollywood Werewolf experience, but that's exceedingly narrow and is largely just a series of normal events broken up by your character chaining themselves up each month.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T02:32:37-07:00","id":1538350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538348#post1538348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe that such a thing exists. Every work is different, and few of them agree. Now, there's the Hollywood Werewolf experience, b<b>ut that's exceedingly narrow and is largely just a series of normal events broken up by your character chaining themselves up each month.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Which as I related many times on this site is basically a similar pitch for early versions of what would become WtA has a similar pitch but the play testers founded it boring so White Wolf changed the concept. <br /> <br /> Also you could easily modify (or at least it's easer than use apocalypse) forsaken for something closely resembling a &quot;move&quot; werewolf experience for the the first few session at least. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538347#post1538347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That and because things were in-house people spoke to one another or just knew the tone they had to hit.<br /> <br /> W5 will forever suffer from trying to be more 'werewolf' and still having the Apocalypse plot required. Because there are times you just want to do 'werewolf' and not 'eternity war.' W5 has the tools to just go werewolf, it should have adventures that give players a traditional werewolf experience.<br /> <br /> But it can't because the apocalypse is tacked on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I wont be surprised if a author would decide to bring back the garou nation the most anticlimactic way possible and have the faction entire personally be written by someone who only skimmed the the fist few sentence of the Western Concordat from WtE at best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T04:37:38-07:00","id":1538352,"title":"","content":"One joke you often hear about the previous editions of WtA is that it's just &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; and there's some truth to it although it's hyperbolic to describe it like that. And if anything, I think it's a far more accurate description for what W5 storylines are like. I think there are two reasons for this: First, it's the W5 design-goal to deemphasize the Umbra and the other are its take on Bane-Spirits.<br /> <br /> W5 has done a lot to discourage players from going into the Umbra. There's the Willpower-damage for being there (which translates into aggravated health-damage if a character runs out of WP), there's the depiction of Spirits being hostile or at least unfriendly to Garou and then the whole Umbra is gatekept behind having to buy a specific Rite first. And so a lot of conflicts aim to be solvable on the physical plane with the Umbra being more like optional content.<br /> <br /> More importantly is the second part which is how W5 treats Bane-Spirits. On pg 244 in the W5 corebook you have this section about &quot;Storytelling with Banes&quot; where it says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Narratively and thematically, Banes always represent something \u2014 they amplify, facilitate, aggravate, and sour what is already there. Which is to say that Banes aren\u2019t responsible for human evil. Tragically, many of a Bane\u2019s victims haven\u2019t even done anything overt to earn their fate. As such, Banes should be symptoms and exacerbating factors in mortal problems rather than their initiators. A serial killer may attract a Bane interested in perpetuating violence and preying upon the bereaved, but a person won\u2019t become a serial killer because a Bane 'made them do it.' </div> </div> </div>On the surface, it might sound like a good idea to not blame human evil on supernatural factors but what's missing there is the animistic perspective/worldview you find in WtA. Spirits and the physical realm influence each other. The way it's formulated in W5, though, the idea is that as long as you have good humans, the Umbra is irrelevant. Say you have this Bane of endless murder but there isn't a single person with a murderous impulse around. By W5's logic, the Bane-Spirit would be irrelevant. Hell, there could be a hundred Bane-Spirits lurking in the Umbra but without any human who already is inclined to be a serial killer, they would be powerless.<br /> <br /> What this leads to is that rather than having this spiritual game where both the Umbra and the physical realm are important in dealing with the Wyrm, in W5 it all starts and ends with human evil. Whenever Fomori turn up in these W5 adventures, it's because they are either bad people or people in a bad situation (like the workers in the warehouse in Scent of Decay). You deal with the former by killing them and you deal with the latter by improving those people's situation. But dealing with the actual Bane-Spirits is entirely optional (I don't know how often I've now already read the phrase &quot;And upon the host's death the Bane-Spirit flees into the Umbra&quot;). And rather than dealing with Wyrm-worshippers, Pentex-subsidiaries trying to spread Wyrm-taint - you deal with bad people doing bad stuff. Oh and by the way, they're Fomori. Instead of the spiritualism, it's all far more mundane. You can also see that in this adventure where when it talks about the rich people who are going to join the hunt, it mentions that none of them are possessed by Bane-Spirits and then adds &quot;At least, not yet.&quot;. Fomori is less about the Wyrm-Spirit in W5 and more code for &quot;This is a bad person.&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's why &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; is far more fitting in this case. Because if you were to get an adventure in the Amazonas Rainforest, you wouldn't get any of the epic battles with Bane-Spirits and Pentex from previous editions, it really would be just about a greedy logging-company doing mundane bad stuff and the managers as well as the security staff all just happen to be Fomori.<br /> <br /> The only other type of storyline is having to deal with other Garou who (because they're too angry and/or sad) are doing the wrong thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T05:12:35-07:00","id":1538354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538352#post1538352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Honesty I think your the type player WtE is tailored to.<br /> <br /> Like the the lead author outright said in they post about the game that the project is ment to appeal to the fans of W20 while streamline info for new players.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>W20</b> fell short of delivering a fully serviceable RPG to it\u2019s Storytellers, however well-intentioned. It had all of the main bones of the setting and stats but no guidance on how to turn it into a game for one\u2019s players. Taking it a step further, some of the writing in this new edition only managed to alienate modern audiences.<br /> <br /> The use of in-character narration to express setting information in prior editions seems an attempt to convey the horror and pathos of the world that would be difficult to get across in stats alone. The information contained in that first-person text is among the most important parts of the setting, but it often fails to convey the true horror of the world of Garou. In many ways the <b>World of Darkness</b> was intended by those who created it to be a place of genuine terror and horror, and not merely \u201csavagery\u201d for its own sake. Horror is a very complex basal guttural emotion that sits in the ganglia, ready to tug the emergency brakes on your body in the presence of what it believes to be a tangible threat. There are many complex higher emotions, but when it comes to the lizard brain, it takes considerable effort to trick it into getting spooked. Invoking a sense of horror in a horror chronicle is a complex enough endeavor that, by and large, these efforts fell short of delivering that experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolf: the Essentials is to serve as a masterclass in using those old tools to introduce new players not just to Werewolf and the World of Darkness on the whole. It gives these important storytelling tools to new and future storytellers in any game, that they might continue genuinely terrifying their players for many more years to come. The passages found in this series can add narrative value to not just Werewolf, or even Vampire and other World of Darkness tables, but also horror writing on the whole. Furthermore, this project aims to streamline the availability of that information and provide guidelines for Storytellers wishing to conduct research using the labyrinthian older editions. </div> </div> </div>Like there's a reason that WtE focuses on the age of heroes that comes after the apocalypse. It's fine to be sad about the death of something you love but it comes the time to move on to something better else you wallow in something you can't get back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T11:43:29-07:00","id":1538380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538348#post1538348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe that such a thing exists. Every work is different, and few of them agree. Now, there's the Hollywood Werewolf experience, but that's exceedingly narrow and is largely just a series of normal events broken up by your character chaining themselves up each month.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a standard popular culture werewolf experience, as I have stated before. It all boils down to what a werewolf IS. Is being a werewolf a curse or a boon? Is the existence of werewolves something unnatural or do they have a place in nature? Is becoming a werewolf something that twists you or is it your true nature? Are werewolves created or born?<br /> <br /> Basically; If a ST wants to run a typical werewolf game, they want a cursed person harmed by being a werewolf and trying to justify their existence. Meanwhile WtA's take is that werewolves are natural and an important part of the world and becoming one is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T11:51:50-07:00","id":1538381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538352#post1538352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>....And you know what? For the exact same reason,too.<br /> <br /> The reason you have the cartoony villains in Captain Planet, is because the creators did not want kids to look at their parents working in polluting fields as monsters.<br /> <br /> W5 moves so much of its guilt away from companies and into bad apples, rather than do what previous editions did and just say the industry itself was the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T15:23:26-07:00","id":1538390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538380#post1538380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically; If a ST wants to run a typical werewolf game, they want a cursed person harmed by being a werewolf and trying to justify their existence. Meanwhile WtA's take is that werewolves are natural and an important part of the world and becoming one is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean <a href=\"https://thelorc.itch.io/what-big-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">What big teeth</a> is basically this game. The player characters are explicitly cursed by an outworldly force and is using they powers to hunt other creatures of nightmare like not-Banes feeding off of negative feelings and other cursed werewolves among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> With the condition that if they kill a human when they're in they wolf form they're irreversibly dammed and will become unplayable if one of they need meter's fill out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538381#post1538381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 moves so much of its guilt away from companies and into bad apples, rather than do what previous editions did and just say the industry itself was the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of a small head project I'd had where the garou has destroyed a wyrm corrupted megacorp and even participated in the death of a Maeljin Incarna.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this still leves 23 other non wrym corrupted megacorp to deal with. Who amoung other things turned time itself into a spendable and more importantly taxable currency, mentally torture a captured eldrich thing to extract it's healing tears, allowing a prosthetic hating cult operating under they name and the Warp trains ... just the Warp train.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like even the clean energy company the garou aligns them selves with isn't the most various guys out there, while they generally wants to improve the world the means they're going to achieve the goal is very questionable to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-11-2024, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T01:00:06-07:00","id":1538413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538390#post1538390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean <a href=\"https://thelorc.itch.io/what-big-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">What big teeth</a> is basically this game. The player characters are explicitly cursed by an outworldly force and is using they powers to hunt other creatures of nightmare like not-Banes feeding off of negative feelings and other cursed werewolves among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Big Teeth isn't really broad enough, though. I mean, it hits the same tones but your character can't be rich or a true monster that eats people.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/177987070427/werewolves\" target=\"_blank\">Maverick Werewolf </a>put it;<br /> <i>&quot;Something that a lot of very modern media seems to lose track of is that <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/182793762717/it-hasnt-ever-really-been-asked-before-no-d\" target=\"_blank\">werewolves are still human, themselves.</a> <b>They are humans with a curse, not just animals or some new alien species with totally different biology and instincts.</b> <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/185397680457/random-werewolf-fact-39-personality-changes\" target=\"_blank\">And their personality doesn\u2019t change.</a> What a werewolf might do would depend entirely on the individual\u2019s personality, not some predetermined \u201cwerewolf instinct\u201d or something to do with packs or whatever. They aren\u2019t animals - they\u2019re people.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And yes, what I am talking about sounds very much like fuzzy vampires. I am aware of the irony. This is why (aside from the previously mentioned locking themselves during full moon) WtA did its turn to animism. But whenever I see people critical of WtA, that's what they mostly mean.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T03:02:13-07:00","id":1538416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538413#post1538413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Big Teeth isn't really<b> broad enough, though</b>. I mean, it hits the same tones but your character can't be rich or a true monster that eats people.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a weird criticism since I suspect that a game based around the classic Hollywood werewolf is very restricting. Like a the core game play loop would problem be uncontrollably rampaging during the full moon and dealing with the aftermath. Like I can see a system based on that loop being used for nice one shots but not much else.<br /> <br /> But if you want something really close to the &quot;classic&quot; werewolf movie tone then I think the Forsaken homebrew <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit#heading=h.nct5jqx4hukj\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf the Cursed</a> is about close as you can get. The wolves of this game is explicitly the result of a supernatural disease and there minimal mentions of animism and the spiret world prevalent in Forsaken and apocalypse besides some vague in-universe theory to the origin of the curse.<br /> <br /> Though one interesting modification I've seen for the homebrew is to explicitly tie the origin of the curse to farther wolf from Forsak. Like the origin of thecurse is the result of a shard of him inhabiting a human host (making the cursed a sort of super spiret touched) and a neat side effect of the curse is that the cursed soul becomes a sort of a spatial black hole that attracts stray souls and usually said souls are the cursed victims...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-11-2024, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T05:02:39-07:00","id":1538420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538416#post1538416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of a weird criticism since I suspect that a game based around the classic Hollywood werewolf is very restricting. Like a the core game play loop would problem be uncontrollably rampaging during the full moon and dealing with the aftermath. Like I can see a system based on that loop being used for nice one shots but not much else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different sort of restriction, there is a vast difference between hiding in your mansion vs in your apartment during the full moon.<br /> <br /> Big Teeth is, to me, less of a werewolf game and more of an allegory.<br /> <br /> Thank you for bringing my attention to Cursed, I have to check that out.<br /> <br /> PS. I like WtA as it is in Legacy. These 'traditional werewolf' posts are more to point out others might want a different experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T06:02:20-07:00","id":1538424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538420#post1538420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Big Teeth is, to me, less of a werewolf game and more of an allegory.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair a lot of media is allegory to some extent. Hell legacy WtA is pretty unsubtle with it's allegory. <br /> <br /> It just that when you compare Big teeth to w5 you find the latter is much more confident with its messaging than the latter and all the better for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T06:36:05-07:00","id":1538426,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to give 5th Edition a fair shake and it keeps making me suspect that it\u2019s being produced by Pentex, not Paradox!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T07:16:11-07:00","id":1538432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538424#post1538424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair a lot of media is allegory to some extent. Hell legacy WtA is pretty unsubtle with it's allegory.<br /> <br /> It just that when you compare Big teeth to w5 you find the latter is much more confident with its messaging than the latter and all the better for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Big Teeth's core gameplay IS the fact that the PCs are poor and struggling. It is a VERY specific story. That's what I mean by it not being broad enough for general werewolf roleplay. Comfortably living or even rich PCs just aren't possible in the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T15:34:13-07:00","id":1538452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538426#post1538426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep trying to give 5th Edition a fair shake and it keeps making me suspect that it\u2019s being produced by Pentex, not Paradox!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna be honest from what I've <a href=\"https://songoftrillium.tumblr.com/werewolfessentials\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf the Essentials</a> is the true 5th edition of WtA.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T19:09:58-07:00","id":1538455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538380#post1538380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a standard popular culture werewolf experience, as I have stated before. It all boils down to what a werewolf IS. Is being a werewolf a curse or a boon? Is the existence of werewolves something unnatural or do they have a place in nature? Is becoming a werewolf something that twists you or is it your true nature? Are werewolves created or born?<br /> <br /> Basically; If a ST wants to run a typical werewolf game, they want a cursed person harmed by being a werewolf and trying to justify their existence. Meanwhile WtA's take is that werewolves are natural and an important part of the world and becoming one is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. I had to explain, from a basement level, massive amounts of why &quot;Lunar Exalted are werewolves&quot; was a good thing, actually, to people with some highly entrenched baggage about werewolves who, when EX3 was under development, were highly concerned about what that meant, all because of the &quot;werewolves are cursed&quot; thing. A lot of it involved reminding them that Exalted was made by the same people who had made W:tA.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(And then development became obsessed with witches...)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T00:39:31-07:00","id":1538468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538455#post1538455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware. I had to explain, from a basement level, massive amounts of why &quot;Lunar Exalted are werewolves&quot; was a good thing, actually, to people with some highly entrenched baggage about werewolves who, when EX3 was under development, were highly concerned about what that meant, all because of the &quot;werewolves are cursed&quot; thing. A lot of it involved reminding them that Exalted was made by the same people who had made W:tA.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(And then development became obsessed with witches...)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Did they then go &quot;But that's the Hippie/Captain Planet game! ;_;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T07:32:56-07:00","id":1538477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538468#post1538468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they then go &quot;But that's the Hippie/Captain Planet game! ;_;&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, but it's somewhat difficult to sift through everything to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T17:59:47-07:00","id":1538503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538468#post1538468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they then go &quot;But that's the Hippie/Captain Planet game! ;_;&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it more of a concern that lunar lore is pretty incoherent across the different edition of Exalted especially 1st Ed since they basically an enemy splat that happened to be playable. <br /> <br /> As far as I know there's little discussion that compares lunar to the garou besides Exalted vs wod. Really Exalted community is pretty insulated from the wod. At least in the forum I've visited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T13:14:33-07:00","id":1538533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538503#post1538503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it more of a concern that lunar lore is pretty incoherent across the different edition of Exalted especially 1st Ed since they basically an enemy splat that happened to be playable.<br /> <br /> As far as I know there's little discussion that compares lunar to the garou besides Exalted vs wod. Really Exalted community is pretty insulated from the wod. At least in the forum I've visited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the day, though, you couldn't hardly go a Lunar thread without someone angrily making exactly that comparison. And that meant it was widespread and continuous, because every thread was a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> Just like this one is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T14:05:41-07:00","id":1538538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538533#post1538533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back in the day, though, you couldn't hardly go a Lunar thread without someone angrily making exactly that comparison. And that meant it was widespread and continuous, because every thread was a Lunar thread.<br /> <br /> Just like this one is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can see it happening in the 1e days when exalted was explicitly the pre history of world of darkness.<br /> <br /> But currently the only talk that links lunars to garou in the forums I've visited are idle speculation of the ebon Dragon being the Wyrm and nothing more substantial than that.<br /> <br /> Really for all I know this phenomenon you're describing is isolated to the exalted section of onyx path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T15:47:01-07:00","id":1538544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538538#post1538538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I can see it happening in the 1e days when exalted was explicitly the pre history of world of darkness.<br /> <br /> But currently the only talk that links lunars to garou in the forums I've visited are idle speculation of the ebon Dragon being the Wyrm and nothing more substantial than that.<br /> <br /> Really for all I know this phenomenon you're describing is isolated to the exalted section of onyx path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but discussions of Lunars and W:tA regarding the thematics raged on for some time. It wasn't about what connections characters directly had as such, but rather what the lens meant for the Lunars and how it should apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T06:17:36-07:00","id":1538648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538381#post1538381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....And you know what? For the exact same reason,too.<br /> <br /> The reason you have the cartoony villains in Captain Planet, is because the creators did not want kids to look at their parents working in polluting fields as monsters.<br /> <br /> W5 moves so much of its guilt away from companies and into bad apples, rather than do what previous editions did and just say the industry itself was the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lack of spiritualism and Garou lore/community robs the game of a lot of opportunities to add more depth to these adventures. And this is part of the bad writing in this adventure particularly. Scent of Decay, the one adventure from the Storytellers Kit with the security guy (who's a Fomor, of course), the crazy Garou from Reclamation, the Fomor from the adventure in the corebook... in all these cases the antagonists have a backstory at least. Here, though, in Red Tundra you got this CEO of the FOMO Hunting company named Olivia Monreau with no personality whatsoever. Just a blank slate Fomor who's doing bad stuff. And really, once you get down to it, that's what's happening in all of these adventures. You have a bad guy doing bad stuff, the PCs become aware of it - and they kill the guy(s). That's all there is to it when you break it down.<br /> <br /> It's not just the way the adventures are set up but that Garou aren't set up in W5 to do anything else. The Umbra is entirely optional and between the old Kinfolk-definition and the Wolf-Blooded in WtF, the Kin-concept in W5 is the weakest and blandest one of those. So when Kin appear in these adventures, it just feels random. &quot;Oh and by the way, that character is a Kin that you can recruit to your Pack.&quot;. The concept is just too broad and vague to be impactful. On one hand, it feels unearned and random who gets to be a Kin and on the other hand, it lacks the impact on the character's life of them either being Kinfolk or a Wolf-Blooded. And that in turn weakens the Garou-PCs connection to humanity. The Touchstone is just gonna be some guy the PC knows/cares about. With V5 it makes sense because it's about remaining human and with H5 it makes sense because the game's about local street-level hunter-cells. But this doesn't work in W5. We see that with the Coach-character in Red Tundra. Because his role in this adventure is to just be the damsel-in-distress who has to be kept out of trouble. And you can't get these humans involved in the combat directly because everything has to be scaled up to be a challenge for a Garou in Crinos-Form.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there are constant references to Garou being a danger to humans around them during their First Change and this fear of Garou going overboard in their violent attacks (resulting in collateral damage). But if you were to take that fear-mongering seriously, human allies are discouraged because then the idea would be instead to treat all humans with connections to Garou like the coach in this adventure. They would all be considered fragile things that need to be protected and kept safe. But that approach seriously limits to what degree human allies and connections can be involved in the adventures of the Garou PCs.<br /> <br /> Going back to the Captain Planet reference, the themes of the game become more toothless as it maneuvered its storytelling into these shallow waters. Both the first adventure in Scent of Decay and this adventure are setting up these straightforward storylines where you have a bad company with bad Fomori at the top and then the Garou-PCs come in, kill the bunch and the company gets shut down. The small towns in question are in even more trouble economically and the Bane-Spirits fled into the Umbra. The ST allows PCs to buy more Renown with XP but it's not like there are big Septs or Moots mentioned in these adventures. At most, a handful of other Garou are even aware of what the PC Pack has done.<br /> <br /> Non-Garou are there to be kept out of trouble and in the dark, Spirits are just a sideshow and all the PCs do is kill bad guys without any other valid alternatives being offered by the game. The game can talk about stuff like it's about &quot;fighting capitalism&quot; and the Age of Apocalypse is the &quot;capitalocene era&quot; but if all that's happening in W5 is just have an ST put bad guys in front of the PCs they then have to kill in the course of the game then there's honestly not a lot going on thematically in W5. Sure, you can dress it up and make it look better than Red Tundra by, for example, giving the antagonist some kind of backstory but from a storytelling perspective it's all about telling, not showing. Because the essential formula doesn't change. You put a bad guy in front of the PCs and expect them to kill the bad guy. You can't maintain interest in the game like that. I think in that context it makes sense to do something like what the Book of Hungry Names has done with its endings. You should be absolutely willing to break the setting and status-quo of W5 to get the story/setting into a better place. Because the core formula/status quo of W5 is boring and bland. You have your group of Garou-PC, you put a bad guy in front of them, they kill the bastard, then you tell them the world is still shit because hey, look, here's another bad guy they gotta kill. And anything that would've interrupted that cycle and would've made things more interesting has been stripped away from the game.<br /> <br /> To end on a more hopeful note, maybe the release of the Shattered Nation supplement will lead to them reintroducing Garou-politics in a bigger fashion since that book focuses on Moots in parts. Maybe they could release adventures again where Garou-politics matter. But right now W5 has a very narrow horizon in what is considered a standard W5 adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T12:15:35-07:00","id":1538667,"title":"","content":"I mean, we knew it would be narrow, we were told constantly that this is 'street level' and not global. So, as you say, you NEED to break the setting to have anything interesting going on.<br /> <br /> Honestly, after perusing an older Forsaken book (wolf's bane), the way that WtF is made interesting is by having a loose canon. Something W5 can't do because it needs to do social commentary, but that social commentary leads nowhere BECAUSE it can't go fully into the Legacy's take. Because corporations aren't all bad??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T18:25:20-07:00","id":1538686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538648#post1538648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game can talk about stuff like it's about &quot;fighting capitalism&quot; and the Age of Apocalypse is the &quot;capitalocene era&quot; but if all that's happening in W5 is just have an ST put bad guys in front of the PCs they then have to kill in the course of the game then there's honestly not a lot going on thematically in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Contrast to what WtE says about the similar situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, the future is uncertain in the face of a Sundered Garou Nation. It\u2019s as likely to succeed as it is to lose everything in the Apocalypse war, emerging everywhere at once under myriad horrifying new faces of evil. For all these many changes and wins for the Garou, their fight against The Wyrm has never been more dire. From humanity making newly destructive moves towards the precipice of climate disaster, to the persistence of Western Colonialism across the globe, the result is more materialized Urge Wyrms than ever before, and many of them bearing new and even more horrifying visages and ideals, representing the absolute worst aspects of humankind. How the splintered Garou respond to this remains to be seen. <b>Bold action, renewal, hope, and valor in the face of impending doom mark the Age of Heroes, where, perhaps for the first time in millennia, the Garou see the potential for anything to happen for those with the chutzpah and gravitas to reach out and grasp it in the fight against the wyrm</b> </div> </div> </div>Tl;dr The would sucks and new Urge Wyrms are born every day because if it. But the garou nation while still reeling from it's near destruction is up to face the challenge and maybe just maybe change the world for the better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538667#post1538667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, after perusing an older Forsaken book (wolf's bane), the way that WtF is made interesting is by having a loose canon. Something W5 can't do because it needs to do social commentary, but that social commentary leads nowhere BECAUSE it can't go fully into the Legacy's take. Because corporations aren't all bad??</div> </div> </div> </div>You know talking about Forsaken, I think there's a lot that W5 could learn from it, Like one defense for W5 I've heard is that W5 disconnect the tribes from ethnic and national organons so that everyone can join. and a response ide give is &quot;Forsaken did that with they tribes and how does that compare to W5?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:24:56-07:00","id":1538831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538667#post1538667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, we knew it would be narrow, we were told constantly that this is 'street level' and not global. So, as you say, you NEED to break the setting to have anything interesting going on.<br /> <br /> Honestly, after perusing an older Forsaken book (wolf's bane), the way that WtF is made interesting is by having a loose canon. Something W5 can't do because it needs to do social commentary, but that social commentary leads nowhere BECAUSE it can't go fully into the Legacy's take. Because corporations aren't all bad??</div> </div> </div> </div>As we've discussed in other threads. For a game that starts with the declaration of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, there's way too little re-imagining happening here to make this work. You don't want the players to go into the Umbra, you don't want them to endanger humans but rather keep them out of trouble and on the sidelines and you don't want them to have epic confrontations with their enemies. Well, there's not a lot left to do if you're gonna stick to the WtA-framework that closely.<br /> <br /> And the anti-capitalist take also doesn't work because if you were to take that idea to its logical conclusion and with so many other avenues taken off the table, you'd have to play the Garou in W5 as outright eco-terrorists. But then of course you got the whole Hauglosk-thing and the Cult of Fenris as a refutation of that idea. So, the core-concept of W5 kinda goes nowhere. It's actually a very similar problem to what you have in H5. That corebook is way too invested in explaining why hunter-orgs and everybody who works for them are bad. But then you follow that core-concept to its logical conclusion and you got a local hunter-cell taking out a monster and... now what? If you stick to the corebook premise of H5, nothing is going on beyond that.<br /> <br /> Both H5 and W5 would be improved by just going out of your way to destroy the setting/status-quo as laid out by their corebooks. Another idea of Book of Hungry Names: Because it's the Age of Apocalypse, lift the Veil and work more closely together with humans. That's not necessarily what I would do with a WtA-games but it's at least something that injects a bit of energy back into the premise.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside... remember that sidebar about animal Touchstones in the W5 corebook? Whoever wrote Red Tundra did do a little setting-breaking themselves by ignoring the corebook (that, for example, feels the need to mention repeatedly that wolves don't live as long as humans) and turning wolves into these human-like characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T10:10:44-07:00","id":1538845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538686#post1538686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know talking about Forsaken, I think there's a lot that W5 could learn from it, Like one defense for W5 I've heard is that W5 disconnect the tribes from ethnic and national organons so that everyone can join. and a response ide give is &quot;Forsaken did that with they tribes and how does that compare to W5?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The tribes in Forsaken work, because they are malleable and more based on broad ideas of tribes. But unlike W5, that doesn't mean that nationalities are removed, rather they are shown in lodges. Lodges in general also allow there to be a variety of ways a werewolf can be, not all of them positive.<br /> <br /> Which leads to;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538831#post1538831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As we've discussed in other threads. For a game that starts with the declaration of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, there's way too little re-imagining happening here to make this work. You don't want the players to go into the Umbra, you don't want them to endanger humans but rather keep them out of trouble and on the sidelines and you don't want them to have epic confrontations with their enemies. Well, there's not a lot left to do if you're gonna stick to the WtA-framework that closely.<br /> <br /> And the anti-capitalist take also doesn't work because if you were to take that idea to its logical conclusion and with so many other avenues taken off the table, you'd have to play the Garou in W5 as outright eco-terrorists. But then of course you got the whole Hauglosk-thing and the Cult of Fenris as a refutation of that idea. So, the core-concept of W5 kinda goes nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD5 has a very strange mentality towards playing morally gray characters. It would be one thing if they were all removed, not a good one but a different one from what we actually have.<br /> <br /> You cannot Second Inquisition/Sabbat/Stargazers/Cult of Fenris/Hunter orgs, but you CAN play a Tzimisce that fleshcrafts their ghouls. You can't play an eco-terrorist, but you CAN play a garou that eats humans or poisons towns. The difference between the man-eaters and Cult of Fenris seem to be less morality (aside from the constant push for CoF to be neo-nazi) and more which 'side' one is on. As long as you are Gaian, you can pretty much do anything within the limits of Chronicle Tenets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538831#post1538831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as an aside... remember that sidebar about animal Touchstones in the W5 corebook? Whoever wrote Red Tundra did do a little setting-breaking themselves by ignoring the corebook (that, for example, feels the need to mention repeatedly that wolves don't live as long as humans) and turning wolves into these human-like characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>As silly as this sounds, having multiple wolf touchstones and wolves being more 'disney' is actually an upgrade. Anything is better than the 'playing lupus is too hard for most' mentality, given that at their most feral lupus are the 'disney' wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T15:10:58-07:00","id":1538871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538831#post1538831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another idea of Book of Hungry Names: Because it's the Age of Apocalypse, lift the Veil and work more closely together with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I could see similar reasoning (the wyrm is using humanities ignorance to it's advantage so we must lift the Veil to educate them)as a legitimate argument by more radical voices in the Eastern Concordant whose whole thing is being more progressive version of the garou nation.<br /> <br /> only held back by the more cautious section (which just so happens to be the Shadowlords) with the counter argument of not having enough Logistics pull to actually properly lift the veil before Pentex bury the message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-18-2024, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T16:35:35-07:00","id":1538879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538538#post1538538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I can see it happening in the 1e days when exalted was explicitly the pre history of world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Making of&quot; book actually describes how that explicit backstory angle was dropped fairly early in development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538455#post1538455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(And then development became obsessed with witches...)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Like, just to put things in perspective, the number of Lunar Charms that include the Protean Keyword, the one that empowers them doing shapeshifting into animal or other human forms, is well over a hundred.<br /> <br /> The number of Charms that use the term &quot;witch&quot; is... five.<br /> <br /> And one of those is a Charm to emulate the mythological character of Circe in doing that forced shapeshifting thing that is the thing that witch is famous for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-18-2024, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T23:35:31-07:00","id":1538889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538879#post1538879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;Making of&quot; book actually describes how that explicit backstory angle was dropped fairly early in development.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It really isn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Like, just to put things in perspective, the number of Lunar Charms that include the Protean Keyword, the one that empowers them doing shapeshifting into animal or other human forms, is well over a hundred.<br /> <br /> The number of Charms that use the term &quot;witch&quot; is... five.<br /> <br /> And one of those is a Charm to emulate the mythological character of Circe in doing that forced shapeshifting thing that is the thing that witch is famous for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel a particularly vital need to shop around for a word that entails how people thought that it wasn't possible to have shapeshifting Charms in Intelligence and Wits. Quite frankly, I find it on par with &quot;We couldn't find the proper adjectives for the Get of Fenris!&quot;, but worse, because people are actually serious when they say it. At least we know that the adjectives thing was a fib to cover up the shit going on with the Fenrir behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> You know claws? Base those on Intelligence, they're for Crafting instead of disemboweling (well, okay, some disemboweling, as a treat). Toxin production? Well, no animal that does this is a particularly good example of an upfront fighter with staying power in a race, you could put that in Intelligence, too. I know what you're going to say; isn't that what the Keyword Attribute swap was for? Well, maybe it wasn't all that vital to have that Keyword in the first place and you were just taking too many cues from the Lunars 2e Charm structure, which is, quite frankly, a baffling sentiment full of infinite celestial wine fountains. And then, at least according to what fan Charm cascades for EX3 Lunars indicated, Argent Weaver Art just isn't there. You could make some neat branching Intelligence and Wits Charms from that, and also production of nacre, ink, and other substances. Use silk to bandage wounds and help them to heal, use nacre to keep a limb stuck on, use ink to make a glob in the water that reacts to the presence of demons like omen weather. Have crafting involve repurposed natural weapons, or take advantage of being able to become legendary size. Don't limit yourself by assuming it can't be done, and don't go straight to psychic surgery if you can exactingly target parasites at an internal medical problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T01:53:54-07:00","id":1538893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538845#post1538845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot Second Inquisition/Sabbat/Stargazers/Cult of Fenris/Hunter orgs, but you CAN play a Tzimisce that fleshcrafts their ghouls. You can't play an eco-terrorist, but you CAN play a garou that eats humans or poisons towns. The difference between the man-eaters and Cult of Fenris seem to be less morality (aside from the constant push for CoF to be neo-nazi) and more which 'side' one is on. As long as you are Gaian, you can pretty much do anything within the limits of Chronicle Tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrast that to WtE spitting the nation to two competing pollical blocks and by all indications from the preview materials the conflict between them is going to be one of the main driving themes in the game. <br /> <br /> From the Eastern Concordat progressive goals of giving the Kinfolk a greater voice in the nation:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eastcons happily use the information and power they wield to hold space for humans, especially those who could deeply impact the world around them. This faction urges a stronger and more thorough integration of Kinfolk into Garou society as warriors, healers, and visionaries, much like the Dawn Tribes. They do not want to hide their Kinfolk away, keeping them from the world with the excuse of protecting them. Instead, Eastern Concordat members wish to teach and prepare their Kinfolk, giving them knowledge and tools to take a more active role in the world in which they live, embracing the ways and guidance of the Hearthbound to integrate kin into their societies. Through their kin, the Eastern Concordat actively seeks influence in the mortal halls of power, leveraging humanity itself to benefit Gaia and all her children. Eastcons believe that keeping up with the modern era is of import. Stagnation is another form of corruption, and by refusing to change with the world around them, the Garou have let this corruption take root and fester. Only by learning and growing can they embody the balance they seek to forge anew in the Triat </div> </div> </div>contrasted by the Western Concordat adherence to old traditions in uncertain times. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A return to these traditions and the hierarchies they stand on, however, also brings with it the half-scabbed wounds that those hierarchies have wrought upon others in the past. For example, the monarchist bent of the Silver Fangs is in direct opposition to the Dawn Tribes\u2019 philosophy of not bending the knee to kings or colonists. It also causes problems when the more autonomous political system of the Skysingers clash with notions of loyalty to a crown, echoing the historical colonization of Celtic peoples by empire. All of this isn\u2019t to say that the Western Concordat is doomed or useless. It is undeniable that the Western Concordat field some of the most dedicated and loyal warriors around, and the hierarchical nature of the faction means that any one group of these fighters can be dispatched and relied upon to work effectively with little oversight. Many a bane has been defeated and many a powerful formori has been slain before it can wreak havoc by the mobilization of Westcon troops in their territories, and the territories of those that would have them. The Shadow Lords may have once been the tacticians and careful planners of efficiency of the Westcons, but it would be a mistake to assume that all of their abilities and knowledge left with their exodus from the faction. Unity and strength of purpose is what led the Garou Nation out of the Age of Apocalypse with the pleas of courage from High King Albrecht, and so it is no surprise that the Westcons believe those are the things that will lead it to ultimate victory and the revival of Gaia. It would be foolish to say that this faction cannot change, and in fact change is already happening with the different reactions to the Hearthbound and changing times of the Age of Heroes. Traditions will change in order to adapt to different circumstances, and perhaps all it needs is a powerful leader to rise from the newest generation of Garou and seize renown, leading the Western Concordat to true unity, and true strength. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T05:50:53-07:00","id":1539016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538845#post1538845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tribes in Forsaken work, because they are malleable and more based on broad ideas of tribes. But unlike W5, that doesn't mean that nationalities are removed, rather they are shown in lodges. Lodges in general also allow there to be a variety of ways a werewolf can be, not all of them positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of nationalities... Famously they took away those connections for the Tribes in W5 but the funny thing is that this broad allowance of what you could theoretically do with that hasn't shown up so far in any of the adventures. There's all this talk in most of them about how the settings are these generic towns but when a specific region is mentioned it's always North America and when it isn't mentioned, it's still clear that the default-assumption is that the described town is a North American one. They stripped away all that lore and background information to just end up overly focusing on North America again.<br /> <br /> And Red Tundra is also an example of what else has been stripped away: The connection to Native Americans. I was thinking that this adventure could've saved itself a lot of trouble by removing all this needlessly convoluted stuff with the high school, the coach and going to the big city and then coming back... if instead you'd center the story around the Dene people in that area. It makes sense why they would have a problem with this hunting-company. You don't even need the fantasy-wolves. That way you could organically tie a lot of stuff together: Garou lore/spirituality and how it ties First Nation beliefs and traditions, the fight against the Wyrm and how that ties to the struggles of First Nation people, the importance of taking care of the land etc.<br /> <br /> But instead, the Dene people are just a footnote in this adventure...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538845#post1538845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD5 has a very strange mentality towards playing morally gray characters. It would be one thing if they were all removed, not a good one but a different one from what we actually have.<br /> <br /> You cannot Second Inquisition/Sabbat/Stargazers/Cult of Fenris/Hunter orgs, but you CAN play a Tzimisce that fleshcrafts their ghouls. You can't play an eco-terrorist, but you CAN play a garou that eats humans or poisons towns. The difference between the man-eaters and Cult of Fenris seem to be less morality (aside from the constant push for CoF to be neo-nazi) and more which 'side' one is on. As long as you are Gaian, you can pretty much do anything within the limits of Chronicle Tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets even more complicated when you include the Pack from Scent of Decay that served the Horned Serpent by deliberately letting the Wyrm run rampant in a town. And they suffered from neither Hauglosk nor Harano, so how does that even work...? W5 is so confused on this point. If it's all just chaos and any Garou could be considered a bad guy based on individual choices, then the Cult of Fenris can't be particularly bad. If Oakheart who's suffering from Hauglosk in this adventure is just a bit of a troubled ally, then why wouldn't the same apply to the Cult of Fenris? It feels like you're running just in circles trying to figure out what W5 considers to be good and bad when it comes to Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538845#post1538845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As silly as this sounds, having multiple wolf touchstones and wolves being more 'disney' is actually an upgrade. Anything is better than the 'playing lupus is too hard for most' mentality, given that at their most feral lupus are the 'disney' wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>And at least this will help people to dismiss the description from the corebook of wolves just looking like big dogs<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T06:54:27-07:00","id":1539018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539016#post1539016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of nationalities... Famously they took away those connections for the Tribes in W5 but the funny thing is that this broad allowance of what you could theoretically do with that hasn't shown up so far in any of the adventures. There's all this talk in most of them about how the settings are these generic towns but when a specific region is mentioned it's always North America and when it isn't mentioned, it's still clear that the default-assumption is that the described town is a North American one. They stripped away all that lore and background information to just end up overly focusing on North America again.<br /> <br /> And Red Tundra is also an example of what else has been stripped away: The connection to Native Americans. I was thinking that this adventure could've saved itself a lot of trouble by removing all this needlessly convoluted stuff with the high school, the coach and going to the big city and then coming back... if instead you'd center the story around the Dene people in that area. It makes sense why they would have a problem with this hunting-company. You don't even need the fantasy-wolves. That way you could organically tie a lot of stuff together: Garou lore/spirituality and how it ties First Nation beliefs and traditions, the fight against the Wyrm and how that ties to the struggles of First Nation people, the importance of taking care of the land etc.<br /> <br /> But instead, the Dene people are just a footnote in this adventure...</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure is funny how they removed cultural connections to be more inclusive and how 'everyone can now be everything', yet as you say the examples are all set in the US and now don't even have any ties to the people of Turtle Island.<br /> <br /> And like, as someone not from the US, it does start to gall when the US is treated as the default location. Especially since Paradox is located in Sweden and Sweden (and Finland) already have PLENTY of material for a wolf hunt focused game.<br /> <br /> It reminds me so much of the time when I suggested that an online game could be set outside the US. I got told this; &quot;The American players would not be able to handle the gun laws being different.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T10:13:33-07:00","id":1539038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539018#post1539018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sure is funny how they removed cultural connections to be more inclusive and how 'everyone can now be everything', yet as you say the examples are all set in the US and now don't even have any ties to the people of Turtle Island.<br /> <br /> And like, as someone not from the US, it does start to gall when the US is treated as the default location. Especially since Paradox is located in Sweden and Sweden (and Finland) already have PLENTY of material for a wolf hunt focused game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extra hilarious because of the complaints from the rest of the world, particularly Europe, about how US-centric the WoD's writing was back in the day. Or perhaps Paradox is pulling a case of sweating while saying &quot;Pay no mind the problems here at your new home!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It reminds me so much of the time when I suggested that an online game could be set outside the US. I got told this; &quot;The American players would not be able to handle the gun laws being different.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's a really weird take. Shadowrun sets missions on an official, almost tournament-like schedule across multiple continents where the weapon laws are all different, but the US-native fans don't seem to have a problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T11:47:24-07:00","id":1539047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539038#post1539038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really weird take. Shadowrun sets missions on an official, almost tournament-like schedule across multiple continents where the weapon laws are all different, but the US-native fans don't seem to have a problem with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was years ago, so maybe it was a different crowd. But then again, Shadowrun is more fiction than WoD is. It could be that people accept gun laws in a constructed setting vs one layed on top of the real world easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T14:42:30-07:00","id":1539054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539047#post1539047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was years ago, so maybe it was a different crowd. But then again, Shadowrun is more fiction than WoD is. It could be that people accept gun laws in a constructed setting vs one layed on top of the real world easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonetheless, it operates on a default of lax gun laws that get way more stringent and restrictive when you move out of the assumed stomping ground of North America, so it's not really that different of a move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T02:12:32-07:00","id":1539090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539016#post1539016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's all this talk in most of them about how the settings are these generic towns but when a specific region is mentioned it's always North America and when it isn't mentioned, it's still clear that the default-assumption is that the described town is a North American one. They stripped away all that lore and background information to just end up overly focusing on North America again.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539038#post1539038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Extra hilarious because of the complaints from the rest of the world, particularly Europe, about how US-centric the WoD's writing was back in the day. Or perhaps Paradox is pulling a case of sweating while saying &quot;Pay no mind the problems here at your new home!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough the authors of WtE also explicitly limits it's focuses to the US pacific north west during the start of the project. With the explicit reasoning that it cuts down on research of need to represent the local tribes relation ship with the garou in more detail with rather limiting them to hundreds of token mentions .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>This week for Werewolf Wednesday we're sharing some insight into localizing settings.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> W:tE will be focused around the Pacific Northwest of the United States. This may seem limiting, but we feel it's important to keep our scope rather small starting off. Rather than offering a lukewarm representation of hundreds of global cultures we don't know as well, we'll provide tools for ST's to integrate local history and legends into their stories. Our hopes are that this results in more vibrant and nuanced cultural representation. Its meant to give one the means to examine their own locale and see what a Gaian community existing alongside their own culture might look like.<br /> <br /> A big opportunity afforded with the Age of Heroes is that, we don't have to ignore the old lore and history in order to make a more inclusive depiction of what the changes in one's locale would be like. Each individual table can hold on to the lore most important to their chronicles, keeping what works for them, and dropping (or progressing) the rest to reflect more modern sensibilities.<br /> <br /> The end goal is to make the setting more holistically timeless, so the game, premise, and chronicles can hold as much relevance now as it can in, say, 20 years from now.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T10:42:36-07:00","id":1539104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539090#post1539090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Funnily enough the authors of WtE also explicitly limits it's focuses to the US pacific north west during the start of the project. With the explicit reasoning that it cuts down on research of need to represent the local tribes relation ship with the garou in more detail with rather limiting them to hundreds of token mentions .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the main author of WtE is also willing to listen if you point out some cultural aspects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, WtE is a FAN project FROM the area they are focusing on. W5 is a book made by a hired team from variety of cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T18:35:53-07:00","id":1539124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539104#post1539104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, WtE is a FAN project FROM the area they are focusing on. W5 is a book made by a hired team from <b>variety of cultures.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes I could Clearly see it in the text of the &quot;high quality&quot; adventures the varied NPC casts that consist of generic student activist on 1# or sad white guy . <b>/s</b><br /> <br /> But You're right the WtE team has to limit they scope of the project because the majority of the team is located in the pacific north west and subsequently are more comfortable with writing and researching about the local cultures. Of cause the main reason that the team limit them selves to native cultures that they can conceivably research is so they can write about said cultures with some degree of delph rather than regulate them to some foot note.<br /> <br /> Like this situation:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539016#post1539016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of nationalities... Famously they took away those connections for the Tribes in W5 but the funny thing is that this broad allowance of what you could theoretically do with that hasn't shown up so far in any of the adventures. There's all this talk in most of them about how the settings are these generic towns but when a specific region is mentioned it's always North America and when it isn't mentioned, it's still clear that the default-assumption is that the described town is a North American one. They stripped away all that lore and background information to just end up overly focusing on North America again.<br /> <br /> And Red Tundra is also an example of what else has been stripped away: The connection to Native Americans. I was thinking that this adventure could've saved itself a lot of trouble by removing all this needlessly convoluted stuff with the high school, the coach and going to the big city and then coming back... if instead you'd center the story around the Dene people in that area. It makes sense why they would have a problem with this hunting-company. You don't even need the fantasy-wolves. That way you could organically tie a lot of stuff together: Garou lore/spirituality and how it ties First Nation beliefs and traditions, the fight against the Wyrm and how that ties to the struggles of First Nation people, the importance of taking care of the land etc.<br /> <br /> <b>But instead, the Dene people are just a footnote in this adventure...</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Is exactly what the WtE team wants to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T23:38:17-07:00","id":1539368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539016#post1539016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 is so confused on this point. If it's all just chaos and any Garou could be considered a bad guy based on individual choices, then the Cult of Fenris can't be particularly bad<b>. If Oakheart who's suffering from Hauglosk in this adventure is just a bit of a troubled ally, then why wouldn't the same apply to the Cult of Fenris?</b> It feels like you're running just in circles trying to figure out what W5 considers to be good and bad when it comes to Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it would be amusing that next time the cult of Fenris shows up there would be a side bar mentioning that they purged all members who expresses human politics from they ranks to maintain garou purity. With large emphases placed on Nazism being the major example. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-27-2024, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T15:51:59-07:00","id":1539445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538845#post1538845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot Second Inquisition/Sabbat/Stargazers/Cult of Fenris/Hunter orgs, but you CAN play a Tzimisce that fleshcrafts their ghouls. You can't play an eco-terrorist, but you CAN play a garou that eats humans or poisons towns. The difference between the man-eaters and Cult of Fenris seem to be less morality (aside from the constant push for CoF to be neo-nazi) and more which 'side' one is on. As long as you are Gaian, you can pretty much do anything within the limits of Chronicle Tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the design intent is simply about blocking off certain groups from being played by players. So the designers start the design process off first by saying, &quot;We don't want people playing Sabbat, or Get of Fenris (or whatever)&quot; and the explanation as to why you can't play that comes later. So with Vampire they walled off the Sabbat because they want to focus on the Anarchs and Camarilla and allowing players to be Sabbat doesn't work within that concept. With W5, the lead designer had a personal dislike for the Get of Fenris and wanted to make them NPC villains, and then the explanation for why you can't play them came about later in the design process. <br /> <br /> Noteably in none of those cases (or in the Stargazers, Second Inquisition, Hunter orgs, etc) does morality play any sort of role. You can play a monstrous flesh-crafting Tzimisce, you just can't play one that's part of the Sabbat. You can play some asshole man-eating werewolf, you just can't play someone that's part of the Cult of Fenris. It's not because those groups are evil, it's simply that the game designer doesn't want you playing members of those groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T17:32:20-07:00","id":1539449,"title":"","content":"The timeline events all but screams that &quot;Can't play Fenrir&quot; and the reason given as to why were immediately concurrent. Later excuses had to come in only to finesse the language so that it only technically hinted at what was going in the writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T19:32:03-07:00","id":1539451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539445#post1539445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . With W5, the lead designer had a personal dislike for the Get of Fenris and wanted to make them NPC villains, and then the explanation for why you can't play them came about later in the design process.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah though an odd thing I noticed is that the cult didn't actually pop up much in the offical adventures as antagonists. Like most of the antagonist we come across in the published adventures are either lone bane corrupted garou or bane corrupted humans working for not Pentex.<br /> <br /> Like the only media I remember the cult showing up in force is book of Hungry Names and even then focus shifts away later in the game when the spirt stuff tankes center stage. Hell one could argue that the ghost council did more damage in the adventures they ahowed up in than CoF...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T20:17:40-07:00","id":1539454,"title":"","content":"CoF have shown up in the majority of Renegade adventures and the Core adventure. Have the Spirals shown up at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T21:03:53-07:00","id":1539455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539454#post1539454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoF have shown up in the majority of Renegade adventures and the Core adventure. Have the Spirals shown up at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not really from what I've seen? Like drug dealer in reclamation is explicitly a lone wolf corrupted by a bane, the corpo suit from red tundra is acting on an existing grudge agenst the garous and don't forget the whole mess with the ghost council letting the wyim sprets loose in the third act of Scent Of Decay apparently because they patron ordered them to and then study the after effects.<br /> <br /> Like all of the those adventures has a noticeable absence of the CoF...<br /> <br /> I would bet my two cents that If the CoF did show up then they would be regulated to angry road blocks for the actual big bads to hide behind rather than the main antagonist driving the plot. Which funny enough is the exact same role the BSD too from time to time,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-29-2024, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T22:51:38-07:00","id":1539456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539445#post1539445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noteably in none of those cases (or in the Stargazers, Second Inquisition, Hunter orgs, etc) does morality play any sort of role. You can play a monstrous flesh-crafting Tzimisce, you just can't play one that's part of the Sabbat. You can play some asshole man-eating werewolf, you just can't play someone that's part of the Cult of Fenris. It's not because those groups are evil, it's simply that the game designer doesn't want you playing members of those groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the what both Second Inquisition and Sabbat books say. In their introduction, they state that SI and Sabbat are not playable because of what they do. Same with Cult of Fenris in the W5 core, it is heavily implied they are not playable because they are worse than other garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T01:44:14-07:00","id":1539458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539445#post1539445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the design intent is simply about blocking off certain groups from being played by players. So the designers start the design process off first by saying, &quot;We don't want people playing Sabbat, or Get of Fenris (or whatever)&quot; and the explanation as to why you can't play that comes later. So with Vampire they walled off the Sabbat because they want to focus on the Anarchs and Camarilla and allowing players to be Sabbat doesn't work within that concept. With W5, the lead designer had a personal dislike for the Get of Fenris and wanted to make them NPC villains, and then the explanation for why you can't play them came about later in the design process.<br /> <br /> Noteably in none of those cases (or in the Stargazers, Second Inquisition, Hunter orgs, etc) does morality play any sort of role. You can play a monstrous flesh-crafting Tzimisce, you just can't play one that's part of the Sabbat. You can play some asshole man-eating werewolf, you just can't play someone that's part of the Cult of Fenris. It's not because those groups are evil, it's simply that the game designer doesn't want you playing members of those groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the most interesting aspects of this mindset is how it provided no benifit to players, the game or the product as a commercial enterprise it simply cultivated a massive amount of ill will from Sabbat and get fans with no meaningful gain.<br /> <br /> Cui bono?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-29-2024, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T01:56:53-07:00","id":1539459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539456#post1539456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the what both Second Inquisition and Sabbat books say. In their introduction, they state that SI and Sabbat are not playable because of what they do. Same with Cult of Fenris in the W5 core, it is heavily implied they are not playable because they are worse than other garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that certain groups were walled off as NPCs because playing one would come into conflict with the core game themes (like Hunter Orgs) or because the lead developer didn't like the group (Fenrir).<br /> <br /> Like with the Sabbat, V5 is intended to be street level personal horror about punks fighting the establishment. Sabbat PCs as nomadic packs of psychos just doesn't fit into the intended V5 playstyle. Same thing with Hunter Orgs, the Hunter play experience isn't intended for players to be part of a big organization with tons of support. <br /> <br /> W5 is a bit different though because the playstyle of a pack of player Fenrir isn't going to be that much different from a regular hame. Fenrir mostly do the same thing any other werewolf PC could do - again cannibal PCs are okay. The big difference between the Cult of Fenris and groups like the Sabbat or Hunter orgs is that the lead werewolf designer has personal reasons for not liking the Fenrir and wanted to wall them off as NPC villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T02:57:38-07:00","id":1539461,"title":"","content":"Repost because editing caused the spam bug;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539459#post1539459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 is a bit different though because the playstyle of a pack of player Fenrir isn't going to be that much different from a regular hame. Fenrir mostly do the same thing any other werewolf PC could do - again cannibal PCs are okay. The big difference between the Cult of Fenris and groups like the Sabbat or Hunter orgs is that the lead werewolf designer has personal reasons for not liking the Fenrir and wanted to wall them off as NPC villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was unclear what I meant. In both Second Inquisition and Sabbat books, we are told that both factions are not playable because they are terrible people. SI are all religious zealots with no one of empathy among them and the Sabbat are a destructive cult which does bad things.<br /> <br /> The same mentality is used for Hunter Orgs and CoF. Hunter Orgs are stated to be worse than typical hunters and are presented as comically inept, even a group based on real-life freedom fighters who are trying to stop illegal sex tourism in their country. The Cult of Fenris are painted as the worst of werewolves, even worse than BSDs (who DON'T suffer from Hauglosk for some reason) who are doing things the WRONG way.<br /> <br /> With SI and Sabbat, it should be noted that the books don't go &quot;These factions do not fit the scope of the game and therefore are unplayable.&quot; They go &quot;These people are oppressing the PCs and are bad people who do bad things and so are not playable.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is my issue, the explanations given are based on morality and yet the PCs are allowed to be even more rotten. So it rings very hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T03:11:59-07:00","id":1539462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539456#post1539456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the what both Second Inquisition and Sabbat books say. In their introduction, they state that SI and Sabbat are not playable because of what they do. Same with Cult of Fenris in the W5 core, it is heavily implied they are not playable because they are worse than other garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnlely enough even WtE is guilty of this since in lore the Star Gazers was absorbed into the Children of Gaia during or shortly after the formation the Eastern Concordat. Though I'd assume that a Children of Gaia character would have access to some of the Star Gazers gifts so they could at least roleplay a wolf that still identified heavily as a star gazer if the want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the whole split between the western and eastern Concordat. Like the team could easy casted the conservative Western Concordat out as bunch of self distractive regressive pricks and that's why you shouldn't play them but in the preview material I got both Concordats are presented as equally viable options for player characters, though the narrative dose have a bit of bias towards the <br /> eastern Concordat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T03:34:18-07:00","id":1539463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539462#post1539462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funnlely enough even WtE is guilty of this since in lore the Star Gazers was absorbed into the Children of Gaia during or shortly after the formation the Eastern Concordat. Though I'd assume that a Children of Gaia character would have access to some of the Star Gazers gifts so they could at least roleplay a wolf that still identified heavily as a star gazer if the want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also the whole split between the western and eastern Concordat. Like the team could easy casted the conservative Western Concordat out as bunch of self distractive regressive pricks and that's why you shouldn't play them but in the preview material I got both Concordats are presented as equally viable options for player characters, though the narrative dose have a bit of bias towards the<br /> eastern Concordat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love WtE, it is still a fan project. A GOOD fan project, but the resources it has are very different from what Paradox/Renegade had for W5. WtE can do stuff that the actual books cannot (even if they should) because it has no corporate oversight.<br /> <br /> Having official books that cost 20+ euro per pop go &quot;You cannot play X because they are NAUGHTY, but you CAN play this worse person&quot; is bad planning and communication between the team. If book A says that faction X is not playable because they are bad, then book Q should not include group \u00d6 that does worse things than faction X as playable.<br /> <br /> I mean, we are 3+ adventures wiser and they still cannot decide on a tone for W5 or how to depict Hauglosk XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T05:01:25-07:00","id":1539464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539463#post1539463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I love WtE, it is still a fan project. A GOOD fan project, but the resources it has are very different from what Paradox/Renegade had for W5. WtE can do stuff that the actual books cannot (even if they should) because it has no corporate oversight.<br /> <br /> Having official books that cost 20+ euro per pop go &quot;You cannot play X because they are NAUGHTY, but you CAN play this worse person&quot; is bad planning and communication between the team. If book A says that faction X is not playable because they are bad, then book Q should not include group \u00d6 that does worse things than faction X as playable.<br /> <br /> I mean, we are 3+ adventures wiser and they still cannot decide on a tone for W5 or how to depict Hauglosk XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that begs the question. If a fan project offers higher quality writing, more coherent lore and actually cares about the themes of a of a franchise you used to like rather than a bastardized version of it diluted who knows how many passes of some focused group and helmed by someone who seems hate the franchise to they very core, While being in all likelihood cheaper that the actual peace of media that inspires it.<br /> <br /> What's the point of sticking with the official media in the first place?<br /> <br /> Also by god some one needs to write a thread for WtE. I don't trust my self doing it since I'll just half ass with a opening post that consistent of the copy and paste paste the author statement of intent and nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-29-2024, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T09:13:05-07:00","id":1539481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1539461#post1539461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <di