izuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T04:25:53-07:00","id":1539841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538031-w5-red-tundra-review?p=1538432#post1538432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Big Teeth's core gameplay IS the fact that the PCs are poor and struggling. It is a VERY specific story. That's what I mean by it not being broad enough for general werewolf roleplay. Comfortably living or even rich PCs just aren't possible in the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if you wanted to be rich and comfortable you\u2019d be playing a hobbit, not a werewolf!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, BIG TEETH does look quite fun, in an Edgar Wright/Simon Pegg/Nick Frost WITH WEREWOLVES sort of way.<br /> <br /> I wonder what the werewolf situation outside Great Britain looks like in this setting? (Also, one wonders what Llanwelly, from THE WOLF MAN (1941) would look like in this setting).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}